  "risk": "high",
  "scope": "Batch 3 (AI Product Editor and Maintainer), development only. All three phases (Work Packages A to G): existing GitHub repository or ZIP connection, commit-keyed code map, safe AI change execution with isolated real tests, bounded repair, durable revisions and stacked follow-ups, draft-PR delivery and export, the Existing project workspace tab, and certification (Golden A to L, negative matrix). Extends the existing SoftwareAgent tool-host contract, sandbox runtime and atomic GitHub writer; adds no scheduler or runtime. Integration milestone 2026-10-29: main merged; each change now runs as a canonical durable run (same outbox, Cloud Run Job claim, run attempt, cancellation and terminal authority). Commands execute only through the existing canonical sandbox seam, and the run's own attempt-bound execution state holds the exact working files, so no authority is manufactured. Live Google execution is not yet exercised. Browser verification of visual changes is wired through the canonical seam; a styles or markup change is verified only when a browser observed the page. Retention: finished changes are removed after 90 days or beyond the newest 50 per linked project when another change is requested; unfinished changes and anything a running change builds on are never removed. Local live check: all migrations apply on a fresh local Supabase stack, the four tables deny anon and signed-in users, and the real Supabase stores pass an ownership, retention and unlink check (scripts/batch3/local-supabase-check.ts). Live GitHub check on one disposable repository (scripts/batch3/live-github-check.ts): real reads, a real draft pull request that was then closed and deleted. Fixed: root-level files located by the code map are now authorised for writing. Live model check: the real coding route changed a disposable repository through a draft PR for about $0.013. Fixed in the shared model adapter: streamed tool-call argument fragments were filed under the wrong key, so tools always received empty input.",
